  {
   "id": "crush-stdlib-md-19",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "## Other families\n\nAlso in the standard library: `bytes.*` (`from_string`, `to_string`, `len`,\n`slice`), `buffer.*` (`alloc`, `read`, `write`, `freeze`), `binary.read_*` /\n`binary.write_*` (u16/u32/u64, big/little endian), `result.*` (`ok`, `err`,\n`is_ok`, `unwrap` — results are plain `{ok, value}` objects), `text.sort`,\n`text.uniq`, `time.format`, `time.parse`, `env.os`, `env.arch`, and the `system.*`\nhelpers implemented in Crush itself (`crates/crush-lang-sdk/sbl/`).\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-stdlib-10",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "print(result.unwrap(result.ok(5)))\nprint(result.ok(5))\nprint(result.is_ok(result.err(\"no\")))\nprint(str.format(\"Hello {}!\", \"World\"))\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
